Comment.13:
03/Apr/2026 13:16;nj814;3 new server are ready for adding roles 

GS enforce  us to set =>
 * [R7C-228025|https://81cdb72c.internal/browse/R7C-228025] Ensure *nosuid* option set on /var partition
 * [R7C-228026|https://81cdb72c.internal/browse/R7C-228026] Ensure *nodev* option set on /var partition

This conflicts with the installation of the Cloudera software on a server, 
{color:#de350b}*If "nosuid &* *nodev" for /var is active during Cloudera installation the server becomes inoperable !*{color}
See Cloudera Support Case [1153245|https://41029392.internal/s/detail/500Ui00000sCkMYIA0][ Inspect Hosts failed|https://41029392.internal/s/detail/500Ui00000sCkMYIA0]


Performing a remount, with the target to enhance the ansible playbooks, fail as well.
The remount command was executed successfully, but the mount has still nosuid and nodev enabled. Just reboot solve this problem.

For future installations, I just see a
 * change of */etc/fstab* 
from:

{code:java}
/dev/mapper/rootvg-varlv /var xfs nosuid,nodev 0 0 {code}
to
{code:java}
/dev/mapper/rootvg-varlv /var xfs nosuid,nodev 0 0 {code}
 * reboot server 

 * install Cloudera software 

 * revert */etc/fstab* 

 * reboot 

This is successfully test on servers dwhazthad[7-9].;;;

